<title>JAPAN: M'bishi Chem plans 10 bln yen U.S. sweetener plant.</title>
<headline>M'bishi Chem plans 10 bln yen U.S. sweetener plant.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Chemical Corp said on Tuesday it plans to spend almost 10 billion yen to build a plant in the United States to produce erythritol, a low-calorie food sweetener.</p>
<p>The plant will have a yearly capacity of more than 20,000 tonnes, the company said in a statement.</p>
